{
  "id": "COMPOUND:34751 - PROTEIN:6256",
  "verbalization": "Withalongolide J is implicated in the targeting of M-phase phosphoprotein 8, which is a key component in the cell cycle regulation process. This phosphoprotein is subsequently targeted by multiple structurally diverse compounds, including (2S,3S)-2,3-Bis(5-Methoxy-3,4-Methylenedioxybenzyl)Butane-1,4-Diol Diacetate, 3-((1S)-1,5-Dimethyl-4-hexenyl)-6-methylene-1-cyclohexene, (3R)-, and 4-methoxy-4-oxo-2-[(2-oxo-1H-quinoline-4-carbonyl)amino]butanoic acid. All these compounds share a common mechanism of action, targeting a conserved cellular protein that is essential for the regulation of the cell cycle. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Histone H1.0 suggests that the interaction between Withalongolide J and Histone H1.0 is likely mediated through a shared biological process, possibly involving the modulation of chromatin structure or cell cycle progression. The evidence supports a mechanism where Withalongolide J indirectly influences Histone H1.0 through its interaction with M-phase phosphoprotein 8, which may play a role in the regulation of gene expression during the cell cycle.",
